Z||000004||AkursedX||08-23-2001||08:39 PM||||Well you know what my Splitfire Wires look like.  I get good performance out of them. Other good wires are MSD's, Accel's, and Taylor's of course (I think those are probably the best)<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||08-23-2001||08:46 PM||||Nice to see you on AkursedX!  <P>I am probably going to get those Taylor's from Race-Tech FieroShop, they are $95 Canadian ($38 USD from summit if anyone wants to know, pretty cheap!)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||08:56 PM||||I use accell 8.5 M.M. wire and I am happy with them.And yes the spiral core wires are better.High energy levels in the plug wires can cause inductanc crossfire problems.Spiral-core wires will eliminate secondary inductance.||||reg||1
Z||000007||2birds||08-23-2001||11:34 PM||||Taylor Spiro-Pro's.  They allow you to ditch the boot heat shields, they come in red (or whatever color), and the boots don't pull off the wires.  Custom fit, and about $40 from Summit.  Mine lasted 7 years before I found some cuts from chaffing.  They still worked fine. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||08-23-2001||11:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kasdan:<BR><B>Red Magnacore Wires, Red Konrad Distribuitor cap</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aren't the Magnacore wires stupid expensive?  Like about $100US for a set?  Are they worth it?<P>------------------<BR>"God made us brothers.  Prozac made us friends." :D||||reg||1
Z||000009||recluse||08-24-2001||01:03 PM||||i paid $72 i think, with shipping.  After getting a set of $40 accell wires and them making my car miss right after putting them on, i would say the extra $32 is worth it.  You can get other decent wires cheaper, i just like these. <P>Matt 87GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||LarryB||08-24-2001||03:16 PM||||I like the Magnecor KV85's as well. One place that has them is: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com/PontiacFiero.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cyberauto.com/PontiacFiero.txt</A> <P>I forget where I got mine but I paid a bit less than that. <P>The Conrad distributor cap/rotor kit is available at Autozone for about $15, the color matches the red on the upper plenum (and the Magnecors are pretty close too)<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by recluse:<BR><B>i paid $72 i think, with shipping.  After getting a set of $40 accell wires and them making my car miss right after putting them on, i would say the extra $32 is worth it.  You can get other decent wires cheaper, i just like these. <P>Matt 87GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
